+# Reading bookmark-first opening (#582)
+
+PR584 is a draft. The user approved a new UX after the earlier ID-positioning experiment failed: a reopened paused transcript starts WITH its saved canonical entry as the first loaded message. Earlier history is behind Show earlier messages. This is an explicit replacement of the earlier expanded-prefix contract, not a tolerance change. It is outside beta.3 and requires independent exact-head runtime and current-main coverage acceptance.
+
+## Product boundary
+
+A lazy immutable StateObject computes one value-only opening seed per actual mounted full target. Discarded parent initializers, streaming and mounted history reloads do not recompute the seed. The transcript subtree owns reading State; composer/header/draft State remains above it. Initial, retained-tab return, native destination and A/B switch share this boundary.
+
+A valid paused bookmark resolves its canonical visible entry once. An opt-in TimelineWindow starts exactly there, including an existing slice within a long reply; older rows are not prepared. A per-mount cursor remains stable under streaming and reload. Explicit Show earlier/previous-page actions can only move it earlier; Show-in-chat can only widen it. Latest ends the opening boundary and uses the normal bottom path. A removed boundary is cleared on generation replacement and cannot resurrect. This does not write a new ScrollPosition: the mounted reader stays under A’s existing missing-entry offset fallback. A nil predecessor also clears the boundary so Show earlier falls back to the normal widened window. Missing, removed, invalid-slice and old-session opening IDs have the existing deterministic normal-tail/bottom fallback. Grouped-question aliases choose the visible group without mutating the semantic bookmark.
+
+Valid paused openings seed ScrollPosition(edge:.top); following/missing-ID openings seed bottom. The stopped onAppear proxy experiment and opening ID/handoff machinery are removed. There is no implicit ID owner to release at idle. Phase tests therefore assert ZERO active AND idle identity writes, and the real native drag still proves ownership and no late handoff. No Task, paint delay, opacity, animation, guessed numeric offset or UIKit introspection is added.
+
+Show earlier stays inline above the first message and is visible below the pinned banner in the first paused frame. A’s accepted entry-alignment correction can subsequently move that inline control above the viewport; a reader reaches it by a normal native scroll to content top. This is not a missing-inset defect; no banner/content-margin change is included. “At the top” means the canonical entry is the first message below the visible existing header/control/padding. Short bookmark-first content uses top alignment; following content retains bottom alignment. Product A subsequently restores the saved fractional distance using its unchanged six-point contract, retarget and20-attempt/2-second budget. Per-route video must show movement no greater than measured header/padding + saved distance +6pt, with the canonical row remaining at least partially visible as the top row.
+
+Before a prefix-widening State change, capture the real reading position and set the existing restoring/pending-offset guard. Existing preference/consistent-geometry compensation holds that entry's screen position. The test first performs the native status-bar top action and requires the whole earlier control to fit in the public native scroll track below the banner. Its AX label and identifier are unchanged. The new recording must show every subsequent Show-earlier tap and a normal tail arrival within4pt, and eventually prove the older history is reachable. No timing workaround is accepted if it visibly jumps.
+
+## Disclosed test changes
+
+The new Domain/hosted tests replace windowFirstID != canonicalID with equality for paused remounts. The retained shownEntries expansion watermark does not force the older prefix back into a new paused opening. Tests cover sliced/grouped IDs, exact start, no hidden-prefix preparation, preceding-page expansion, missing/session fallback, seed-once identity, mounted reload, hidden reload and target isolation.
+
+The zero-numeric-arrival setup derives a top-position bookmark from real identical-window geometry: distance =0.5 - measured first-entry lowerBound. Every zero-attempt/zero-command/one-save assertion remains. No assumed initialized-ID delivery or guessed height is used. The original ReadingUITests file is re-pinned only to merged #587, and the restoration value tests remain byte-identical. The two deliberate H/S contract-file edits below are separately committed and reviewed; they are no longer claimed byte-identical.
+
+H-r1 exposed two harness assumptions. The hidden-tab/desktop/drop/timeout tests compared raw offsets across a remount; bookmark-first intentionally omits the preceding content, changing the coordinate origin. A separate test-only commit captures the actual saved entry frame before hiding and requires that same entry to intersect the viewport after completion, at the same entry-relative position within the unchanged2pt tolerance. Both raw and relative deltas are logged. Touch ownership, timeout preservation, retry counts, fixed targets and zero hidden timeline work remain unchanged. Missing frames fail, never skip. H-r1 did not record the necessary before/after frames, so its .arrived result is not treated as independent semantic proof.
+
+The identical-history open reload reached .arrived without a command, so H1 was NOT exercised. The revised DEBUG fixture keeps the real normal window open and sends a same-session timeline resync with identical item IDs/order, growing exactly one already-measured message strictly before the bookmark. The bookmarked entry's actual reload displacement must exceed1pt; the first pin must equal the previous actual offset plus that measured displacement within2pt. Only then does the existing delivery refusal inject the normal tail upsert. The pre-tail identities/window/revision and edited-row geometry are checked; real first/hidden/frame changes plus a separately measured tail displacement gate release within10attempts/1second. Only final .arrived, miss<=2pt and the original6pt entry/pixel checks count. Already-aligned/no-command or any missed real-layout gate is H1-not-exercised/STOP, with no timing rescue. The hosted pin-baseline assertion now includes only the measured reload shift; the UI method adds the same explicit checks, leaving every existing pixel2pt/6pt assertion intact. No release product restoration logic changes. A new hosted test still proves bookmark-first remounts keep their first row fixed through a mid-restore tail arrival.
+
+A separate capture correction uses upperBound > offset +0.5pt (shared minimumVisibleExtent) so a numerically touching row is not saved as visible. Value tests cover equal-edge,+0.4,+0.6 and identical restored offsets. A's target correction, tolerances and budget are unchanged.
+
+## Proof and stop
+
+Before any build, QA reviews the cumulative implementation, test diff, source hashes and exact fresh manifest. Fresh guarded build/deinit/policy; three Pro Max recording methods cover all four routes, Show-earlier expansion and short content; separate SE portrait and XXXL portrait paused recordings require first-frame visibility below the banner; landscape is recorded only under the disclosed #483 exclusion; N; original H15/19 and S2; identical additive main/head CPU test overlays (16 scroll steps,100 paused chunks and two fresh 600-row/bookmark-60 openings per side), with paired DEBUG-only hooks observing the actual rendered window’s preparedRowCount. Counts (including deep-open prepared rows and body/timeline) must be no greater than main; process CPU is supporting evidence, flagged non-blocking if more than20% higher with equal counts; original ordered C23/C50; cold R0; Reading SE; D/current-main combined coverage with overlap/conflict review. Device acceptance remains deferred.
+
+The opening/performance/restore gates are independent of eventual AX readiness. Original videos, unaltered full frames with actual presentation timestamps, complete stdout and cleanup receipts are retained on evidence/ux-582. No first-paint claim comes from a screenshot queried after readiness. Every unexpected count/outcome or wrong first content is a STOP, with no assertion retry or timing iteration. The parent owns landing.
+
+## Recording-only fixture correction after F-r1
+
+F-r1 is preserved as STOP evidence, not credited. Its two fixture defects were an offscreen horizontal action strip and a TextView-only composer query. The DEBUG fixture now uses two visible rows of six native controls with short labels and44pt minimum label content, preserving all12 actions. Its controls use a fixed12pt test-only font; product Dynamic Type is unchanged. This adds offered control height and reduces the real conversation viewport; the footage and measured viewport disclose it. No product view, height, header, scroll inset, delay or positioning logic changes for this correction. The new test uses the existing general descendant composer lookup and the same software-keyboard setup sequence as Reading tests.
+
+The branch was rebased onto85ee757a. The full pre-harness cumulative patch is byte-identical to the reviewed a971c9343/77b24899 patch. The one re-pinned original Reading file equals #587 on main; the #588 permission-menu product file is outside #582’s delta. Evidence and fresh configuration are independently reviewed before any build.
+
+
+## Accepted first-frame evidence on5c785b
+
+Independent QA accepted the exact encoded samples for all four routes, SE portrait and XXXL portrait, with bounded A movement and real prepend/tail stability. Only the first line ("Reading…") of the bookmarked message is visible on the first frame. The number 90 only becomes readable after the restore. This is the disclosed XXXL limitation of the recording viewport; landscape remains an uncredited #483 diagnostic. N13 passed. H-r1 STOP and its original results remain preserved; no later gate is credited until the reviewed harness changes pass on their exact head.
+
+
+## Timeout/drag UI coordinate correction and remaining-selector sweep
+
+After H-r2 proved the changed origin, review found the same raw-origin assumption in the second S UI method. The first S attempt was interrupted during the first method's setup/app launch, with no assertion outcome; it is preserved as a partial execution, not a zero-execution refusal or a completed test retry. A process-group exit race in the external runner was manually cleaned and independently reported.
+
+The timeout fixture now exposes the original measured entry ID, frame and relative position through its DEBUG AX value only, preserving its existing visible text and offered viewport. The test retains its initial1200 timeout, real-drag chosen>1300, chosen==actual, completion and held checks. After remount it requires the same measured entry to intersect the viewport, entry-relative position within the unchanged2pt tolerance, and saved bookmark==new actual offset within2pt. It logs both origin shift and relative delta. This deliberately replaces only the two incompatible old-origin equalities; no pixel or six-point reading assertion changes.
+
+The source sweep covers all52 unique selected S/C23/C50/R0/RSE methods across five full files and their helpers, plus the three additive CPU methods. Only the two timeout/remount equalities needed this further adaptation. Reading's rotation/stream/prepend/tab/reopen checks compare public screen frames; CPU paused-stream checks stay within one mount, and deep-open checks are already entry-relative. Exact classified hits and source hashes are stored with the manifest before any new build. All previous runtime evidence remains separate; no S result is credited from the interrupted attempt.
+
+### CPU r8 correction: transcript equality boundary
+
+The r8 comparative CPU gate stopped on a real regression: the extracted transcript projected twice per streamed batch (main once), and deep openings prepared2700 rows versus main2070. An uncredited DEBUG attribution run identified the extra `@self` pass from unchanged parent/header inputs separately from the required `CompanionStore.conversations` pass. The transcript now compares Store identity, target, immutable opening, managed visibility, Show-in-chat request id and captured agent capabilities. Generated builders/actions are excluded only after a transitive capture audit: they read current Store values or persistent parent State storage; the one copied Agent capability set is an equality input. Own Observation, environment, State and restore updates remain live.
+
+Fresh proof repeats the first-frame videos, N16 (including live paused capability grant/revocation, exact once-per-batch projection and same-id Show-in-chat non-replay), H15/19, S2 and actual native archive-header activation before the unchanged main/head CPU bar and broad suites. DEBUG availability samples are the actual row constructor inputs, not a claim of hosted native button activation. The transient attribution instrumentation is excluded from credited builds. No CPU allowance is applied by this change.
